;; Reviewed 2026-10-10 (written by Claude, from design section 15, the
;; RMS and LIB$ manuals, the guest runs and the debugger run; for the
;; user's review). Why this is right:
;; - GIVEN, 256 bytes, is the name given to PocRtl.mar's POC_PARSE and
;;   POC_CREATE_DIRECTORY, as RMS takes at most 255 characters; it is
;;   not exported. pathSeparator is a constant, with no symbol.
;; - EndsDirectory is TRUE for ":" (#58), "]" (#93) or ">" (#62), the
;;   ORs short-circuited. It and Fill are not exported: each is entered
;;   by a .WORD mask and called without G^.
;; - Fill copies dir up to its 0X into GIVEN, FALSE when dir is "" or
;;   255 characters are copied and more remain; then ":" unless the last
;;   character ends a directory (FALSE if there is no room), then 0X,
;;   and the length, SHORT, to the VAR INTEGER (CVTLW, a word under
;;   -O2).
;; - MakePath copies its two value arrays, then puts dir in path up to
;;   LEN(path) - 1, ":" when dir is not "" and does not end a directory,
;;   then name, and 0X when path has room for it.
;; - IsDirectory and MakeDirectory are Fill and then, only when it is
;;   TRUE, POC_PARSE or POC_CREATE_DIRECTORY with GIVEN by reference and
;;   the length by value (CVTWL); the status's low bit is the result
;;   (BICB3 #254).
;; - The trap 2 calls are the index checks; the trap 12 calls after the
;;   last RET of a function are its end without RETURN, never reached.
;;   The initializer only marks the module initialised: it imports
;;   nothing.
;; - In the debugger run, MakePath("SYS$LOGIN", "X.MOD") gives
;;   SYS$LOGIN:X.MOD; SYS$LOGIN is a directory and [.NO-SUCH-DIRECTORY]
;;   is not. On the guest, PlatformOut's MakeDirectory makes [.MADE.SUB]
;;   and [.MADE] above it, and succeeds again when they are there.
; Directories, written by poc (doc/developer/vax-macro32-backend.md)
